<BaseLayout title="MarketPulse — Egemen Özen" description="A locally run portfolio workspace for positions, prices and cost calculations.">
<section class="section"><div class="container case-prose"><a class="text-link" href="/#selected">← Selected work</a><p class="section-label">Product development / Local application</p><h1>MarketPulse</h1><p class="case-subtitle">A local portfolio workspace for bringing positions, transactions and price context together.</p><h2>Problem</h2><p>Portfolio data can be difficult to interpret when prices have different sources, currencies and observation times. The workspace makes the available information and its limits visible.</p><h2>My contribution</h2><p>I built the product using a React and TypeScript interface with a Python / FastAPI backend and a local SQLite database. The implementation includes transaction records, average-cost calculations, price management and a clearly labeled sample portfolio.</p><h2>What I chose</h2><p>Data stays on the local machine. Missing values remain missing, and prices carry source and observation-time information. The application distinguishes sample prices from observed prices.</p><h2>Scope</h2><p>This is a local application, not a public web service. A publicly accessible code repository or demo has not been verified, so neither is linked here. This project does not claim financial advice, real-time prices or investment returns.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/#contact">Contact Egemen about this project ↗</a></p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
